rows.abstract:
Seeks to institute new measures for the NFA to more effectively handle its role of ensuring national food security and stabilizing rice supply and prices, and help reduce poverty, promote social justice, empower the rural sector, improve the productivity and income of agricultural workers and producers, and comply with the Food Safety Act of 2013 (R.A.10611).
Intends to specifically espouse several reforms as follows:
1.	Setting the policy on National Rice Reserve equivalent to at least SIXTY (60) days national consumption requirement to provide Stocks for:  Food Security; Calamities; Marginalized Sector; and Trade/Export (in case of surplus);
2.	Classification of NFA as a Government Instrumentality vested with Corporate Powers (GICP);
3.	Stabilization function for palay and rice;
4.	Retention of NFA´s regulatory function, pursuant to R.A.10611;
5.	Condonation of all NFA´s existing obligations and interest payments.

Seeks to provide for the determination of the beneficiaries of the lifeline rate - the low-income or the marginalized end-users, to ensure that the Lifeline Rate subsidy will truly reach its intended beneficiaries.

Amends EPIRA to provide for a socialized pricing mechanism as follows:

100% discount - electricity consumption not exceeding 20 kwh;
  50% discount - electricity consumption not exceeding 50 kwh;
  35% discount - electricity consumption not exceeding 70 kwh;
 20% discount - electricity consumption not exceeding 100 kwh.

Seeks to institutionalize the Philippine Plan of Action for Senior citizens (PPASC) that will serve as the point of synergy of all efforts directed towards the promotion of the wellbeing of the senior citizens.

Allocates funds for the implementation of programs, projects, activities and services which will address the needs of senior citizens, in either, but not limited to the following:
a.	Information and Communication Campaign and Advocacy (re: aging, and prevention of discrimination against and abuse);
b.	Education, Human Resource Dev´t. and Capability Building (for family members, family caregivers, and professional and service providers);
c.	Protection and Safety Program (friendly facilities in compliance w/ Accessibility Law)
d.	Group Home/Foster Home (for neglected, abandoned and detached);
e.	Policy Development and Legislation (promotion of rights and full participation and equality in the development process);
f.	Employment Opportunities; Advancement of Health and Well-being; Communicty-Based Facilities; and other projects and activities the agencies may implement in relation to their respective mandates.
